  "meta": {
    "probe": "ur-stencil-b",
    "target": "same lineage as ur-stencil, different object: a square record label rather than a poster -- centre hole, ring of catalogue text, matrix numbers, one red mark",
    "method": "the composition is built from circle regions and a ring layout instead of a grid, to test whether the substrate's competence survives leaving the rectangle. It does: circle is a first-class region for solid, and repeat's ring layout places by angle.",
    "notDone": "text cannot be set on a curve -- there is no text-on-path -- so the ring of catalogue type had to become straight lines placed around a circle, which is the one thing on this sheet that a real label would never do"
  },
